{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Change 1 (pass1.py container-stage split) implemented and pushed as Gerrit 1752 (stacked on 1751).\n\n- Extracted llm/plan_review/container_stage.py (296 LOC, in band): CONTAINER_CRITERIA, _CONTAINER_MAX_WORKERS, _too_big_finding, build_sibling_roster, _timed_pairing, _run_container — the exact seam run_pass1 already cut at its lone 'if container and ctx.has_children:' branch.\n- _submit_ctx relocated to generation.py (per the handoff trap #2): the pool worker it launches reads generation's own _CANCEL_SCOPE ContextVar via copy_context(); leaving it in pass1 would force container_stage->pass1 and cycle. Docstring rewritten to the correct rationale (cancel scope is generation-owned; gate-session vars live in gate_context.py).\n- pass1.py: 800 -> 534 LOC; re-exports every moved name (noqa F401), so orchestrator.py / provider_parity.py / eval_solver.py imports and pass1.<symbol> patch/inspect sites are byte-unchanged. generation.py 346 -> 362.\n- Direction one-way: pass1 -> container_stage -> generation.\n\nVerification: make lint + make typecheck green; targeted plan_review/workflow/container suites pass (1027 passed; the only failures in the sweep were 5 PRE-EXISTING env failures in test_bridge_provider_wrappers_heldout.py — confirmed identical on clean origin/main a79ed876b0, unrelated to this change). Test-count PARITY proven delta 0: fresh venv initially collected 24 fewer only because fastapi/httpx/starlette extras were absent (importorskip-gated audit/opcert modules); after installing them, branch collects 12978/13247 == base exactly, with zero branch-only node ids.\n\nChange 2 (push.py split, the push._git core-param trap) next."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126",